 ## 🚀 Building & Running on Ubuntu
 .
 ### System Prerequisites (Ubuntu / Debian)
 ```bash
 sudo apt update
 sudo apt install -y build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev libgtk-3-dev \
     libxcb-render0-dev libxcb-shape0-dev libxcb-xfixes0-dev libxkbcommon-dev \
     libfontconfig1-dev libwayland-dev libx11-dev libgl1-mesa-dev
 ```
 .
 ### Run the Application (Development / Direct)
 ```bash
 cargo run --release
 ```
 .
 ### Install Globally or User-Wide
 You can install the compiled binary directly into your user path:
 .
 **Option A: Cargo Install (installs to `~/.cargo/bin/mysql-rusty`)**
 ```bash
 cargo install --path .
 ```
 .
 **Option B: Copy to `~/.local/bin` or `/usr/local/bin`**
 ```bash
 # Build release binary
 cargo build --release
 .
 # Install for current user:
 mkdir -p ~/.local/bin
 cp target/release/mysql-rusty ~/.local/bin/
 .
 # Or system-wide (requires sudo):
 sudo cp target/release/mysql-rusty /usr/local/bin/
 ```
 .
 ### Desktop Shortcut (Ubuntu Application Launcher)
 To add MySQL-Rusty to your desktop application menu with its application icon
 (using
 [`packaging/linux/mysql-rusty.desktop`](./packaging/linux/mysql-rusty.desktop)):
 ```bash
 mkdir -p ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps
 cp assets/icon.png ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/mysql-rusty.png
 .
 mkdir -p ~/.local/share/applications
 cp packaging/linux/mysql-rusty.desktop
 ~/.local/share/applications/mysql-rusty.desktop
 ```
 .
 ### Use with AI agents (MCP)
 `mysql-rusty` can run as a headless [Model Context Protocol
 (MCP)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) server over `stdio` so Claude Desktop,
 Cursor, or other MCP clients can inspect schemas and run read-only queries
 against any saved connection profile (or the built-in `demo` sandbox):
 .
 ```bash
 mysql-rusty mcp --profile "Local Dev" --max-rows 200
 ```
 .
 Options:
 - `--profile <name|id>`: Saved connection profile name/ID (or `demo`).
 - `--database <db>`: Override the default database.
 - `--max-rows <n>`: Row cap for `run_query` (default `200`, max `10000`).
 - `--allow-writes`: Permit write/DDL statements (disabled by default; profiles
 marked `read_only` always remain read-only).
 .
 Example Claude Desktop / Cursor MCP config:
 ```json
 {
   "mcpServers": {
     "mysql-rusty": {
       "command": "mysql-rusty",
       "args": ["mcp", "--profile", "Local Dev"]
     }
   }
 }
 ```
 .
 ### Run Unit Tests
 ```bash
 cargo test
 ```
 .
 ### Run Integration Tests (MySQL 8 / MariaDB)
 ```bash
 docker run -d -p 3306:3306 -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root mysql:8.4
 MYSQL_RUSTY_IT_HOST=127.0.0.1 MYSQL_RUSTY_IT_USER=root
 MYSQL_RUSTY_IT_PASSWORD=root \
   cargo test db_integration_tests -- --test-threads=1
 ```
 .
 ### Reporting Bugs & Logs
 Daily rotating logs are written to
 `~/.config/mysql-rusty/logs/mysql-rusty.log.YYYY-MM-DD` (or your OS config
 directory). You can open this folder from the Command Palette (`Ctrl+K` →
 **Open logs folder**).
 To capture verbose SQL/AI diagnostic logs:
 ```bash
 MYSQL_RUSTY_LOG=debug cargo run
 ```
 .
 ### Translations
 UI strings are localized via `rust-i18n` in
 [`locales/en.yml`](./locales/en.yml) and [`locales/es.yml`](./locales/es.yml).
 You can switch between **Follow System**, **English**, and **Español** under
 **AI & App Settings → Appearance → Language**. To add a new language, copy
 `locales/en.yml` to `locales/<lang>.yml`, translate the values, and register
 the locale in Settings.
